"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L52"},{"id":"progress_desktop_scope","label":"Desktop Metric Excludes Mobile Scope","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"desktop metric excludes mobile scope","rationale":"The mobile capability and mobile-only `CORE-029` are outside this desktop metric, as stated in [CORE-PLATFORM-001](../../product-contract/capabilities/CORE-PLATFORM-001/SPEC.md). Android/iOS remain supported targets; no desktop requirement or platform is waived.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L16"},{"id":"progress_metric_definition","label":"Implemented Requirements Earn Credit","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"implemented requirements earn credit","rationale":"Only requirements explicitly marked `implemented` in a platform traceability map receive credit. Partial, not-started and missing/unassessed rows receive no credit. Overall sums the three platforms' implemented rows and divides by their combined desktop requirement count.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L14"},{"id":"progress_native_readiness","label":"Native Implementation Readiness","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"native implementation readiness","rationale":"Follow [native implementation readiness](../../product-contract/READINESS.md): Wave 1 filename generation, post-capture actions, region capture and editor session; then editor expansion and the foundation/catalogues. Existing Linux work follows its more specific implementation plan.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L48"},{"id":"progress_not_release_readiness","label":"Coverage Does Not Certify Release","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"coverage does not certify release","rationale":"Requirement labels are unweighted: a catalogue requirement can cover hundreds of items. These values do not certify current CI, native usability, conformance, security/privacy/accessibility review, cross-platform parity, or release approval. A graph edge or test-file presence does not earn implementation credit.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L18"},{"id":"progress_record_execution_evidence","label":"Record Actual Verification Evidence","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"record actual verification evidence","rationale":"- Record actual commands, results, source revision and evidence when tests or target qualification run. This reporting change does not claim a fresh native build or test run.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L51"},{"id":"progress_semantic_refresh","label":"Refresh Graph Semantics After Markdown","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"refresh graph semantics after markdown","rationale":"Refresh affected Graphify semantic graphs after changing these Markdown files. EXTRACTED graph relationships can locate explicit evidence; INFERRED relationships must be verified against source and cannot change these counters.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L65"},{"id":"progress_status_disposition_separation","label":"Implementation Disposition Qualification Separation","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"implementation disposition qualification separation","rationale":"- Keep per-requirement implementation status separate from platform disposition and qualification.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L50"},{"id":"progress_traceability_missing","label":"Missing Maps Are Unassessed","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"missing maps are unassessed","rationale":"The native application is documented as not started. No platform traceability maps currently supply implementation credit. Missing maps mean unassessed requirements, not accepted Unavailable/Not applicable dispositions. Add evidence and traceability as implementation begins.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L24"},{"id":"progress_unassessed_requirements","label":"macOS 324 Unassessed Requirements","_origin":"semantic","community":0,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"macos 324 unassessed requirements","rationale":"- **macOS:** 0 implemented, 0 partial, 0 not started, 324 without a recorded implementation status. [Native platform evidence](README.md).","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L22"},{"id":"readme_implementation_progress","label":"Implementation Progress Report","_origin":"semantic","community":2,"community_name":"macOS Native Pilot","file_type":"concept","norm_label":"implementation progress report","source_file":"README.md","source_location":"L3"},{"id":"progress_ci_freshness","label":"Regenerate All Progress Files","_origin":"semantic","community":3,"community_name":"macOS Progress And Coverage","file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"regenerate all progress files","rationale":"Update the affected requirement maps when implementation, evidence, blockers or dispositions change, then regenerate **all four** progress files in the same checkpoint. Each desktop platform uses `traceability/<CAPABILITY>.json`; Linux currently uses `linux-qt/traceability/`. The manifest supplies requirement IDs and the denominator. New requirements without recorded status automatically receive no credit. CI rejects stale generated files.","source_file":"PROGRESS.md","source_location":"L63"}],"links":[{"source":"readme_pilot_default","target":"readme_pilot_decision","relation":"cites","_origin":"semantic","confiden